  idea    cap the recurrent gain of the gate (sigma_max(W_h) <= 0.5 after every step), or remove the recurrence (GATE_PREV's input only)
  source  batch 14's S39 (at S=8 the stream leaves h as |W_h h_(t-1)| outgrows |W_in v_t|) and S40 (GATE_PREV's input carries the stream, h only partly; 0/10 bound)
  change  CAP: after every optimizer step W_h <- W_h * 0.5 / sigma_max(W_h) if sigma_max(W_h) > 0.5, optimizer state untouched; NOREC: W_h = 0, frozen; nothing else
  arm CAP_M        lr 0.001  iters 28800  seeds 260-269 (10)  — S33's D8_HINGE + CAP (Muon)
                   schedule: Muon lr 0.005: gate W_in/W_h/W_g throughout, other Muon weights x0.1 for updates 1-2400; Adam on embedding and conv 0.0001 for 1-2400, 0.001 after; + main's HINGE hinge; + CAP (sigma_max(W_h) <= 0.5 after every step)
  arm PREV_CAP_M   lr 0.001  iters 28800  seeds 260-269 (10)  — S40's D8_PREV_M + CAP (Muon)
                   schedule: Muon lr 0.005: gate W_in/W_h/W_g/W_prev throughout, other Muon weights x0.1 for updates 1-2400; Adam on embedding and conv 0.0001 for 1-2400, 0.001 after; + main's HINGE hinge; + CAP (sigma_max(W_h) <= 0.5 after every step)
  arm PREV_NOREC_M lr 0.001  iters 28800  seeds 260-269 (10)  — S40's D8_PREV_M with NOREC (W_h = 0, frozen; Muon)
                   schedule: Muon lr 0.005: gate W_in/W_h/W_g/W_prev (W_h frozen at 0) throughout, other Muon weights x0.1 for updates 1-2400; Adam on embedding and conv 0.0001 for 1-2400, 0.001 after; + main's HINGE hinge
  arm PREV_CAP_A   lr 0.001  iters 28800  seeds 260-264 (5)  — S40's D8_PREV_A + CAP (Adam)
                   schedule: gate W_in/W_h/W_g/W_prev 0.001 throughout; every other parameter 0.0001 for updates 1-2400, 0.001 after; + main's HINGE hinge; + CAP (sigma_max(W_h) <= 0.5 after every step)
  pairing seeds 260-269: CAP_M with S33's recorded D8_HINGE; PREV_CAP_M and PREV_NOREC_M with S40's recorded D8_PREV_M; PREV_CAP_A with S40's recorded D8_PREV_A; same initial parameters (NOREC: W_h = 0) and batches; on the 2.10GHz CPU the records were made on
